  "body": "Side branch: side/path-kernel\n\nK4 of the path kernel (#4023): the order stage and the link stage, behind `OrderPlanner` and `LinkProof`. No old planner changes. No planner calls the new code yet, so the output with the default switch is identical.\n\n## What changed\n\nPublic surface:\n- `order::OrderStage` (impl `OrderPlanner`). It resolves Auto, gets the sense of the walk from the region, sets climb or conventional for each curve, and picks the order and the start points. Refusal: `ORDER_NOT_PLANAR`.\n- `OrderedSet::marks()`. `OrderedSet::new` moves each mark of the guide set to the new index of its curve. A stretch on a reversed curve is reversed too. No planner can drop a mark.\n- `link::LinkStage` (impl `LinkProof`). The tool stays down on a proved path, else it lifts with a named reason.\n- `link::Level { made, planned, links }` (`Level::new`, `with_links`). `LinkProof::link` now takes a `Level` instead of `planned: &[Cut]`.\n- Lift reasons: `CUTS_PART`, `HITS_FIXTURE`, `CROSSES_CUT`, `UNCUT_STOCK`, `BAD_PATH`, `NOT_PLANAR_LINK` (and the existing `USER_RETRACT`). Constant: `SWATH` = 0.9. Each lift arm has its own named reason, with no fallback.\n- `camcraft-geometry`: `geo2d::segments_cross`, `segment_gap` and `point_segment_distance`, each with unit tests. The kernel still depends on geometry only.\n\nOrder (`crates/pathkernel/src/order/`):\n- A ring waits for the neighbour rings on the side that the walk comes from (the order of the offset tree, Held 1991).\n- From the ready starts, the walk takes the first one that the link stage can prove. It tries them in this order: curves without a full-width stretch first, then the next run on the chain of the Adaptive air plan (`air_chain::chains`, ported), then the nearest start.\n\nLink (`crates/pathkernel/src/link/`): the stage tries three paths, in order:\n1. The straight chord.\n2. Back along the open cut just made, then a chord to the next start (`air_chain::link`, ported).\n3. A walk along a loop of the centre area (`ring_links::edge_route`, ported).\n\nEach chord must stay in the centre area or the air. It must not touch a planned cut and must not cross a made cut or an earlier link. It may run only over cleared stock: within 0.9 tool radius of a made cut, or in the air of the region. The strip just inside the stock edge is stock as any other: it is open only where the swath of a made cut covers it (review of this PR). If no path is proved, the hop lifts with the reason of the straight chord. The table in `Plan::new` stays the one gate.\n\n## Readings: old against new\n\nMotion `kernel_laws` with the #4154 measures, tool radius 4, step 2:\n\n| Fixture | Kernel lifts / crossing feeds | Old 2D Pocket | Old 2D Offset |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| disc Inside | 0 / 0 | 18, none named / 0 | 0 / 0 |\n| disc Outside | 13, named / 0 | 18, none named / 0 | 0 / 0 |\n| dog bone Inside | 0 / 0 | 26, none named / 0 | 0 / 0 |\n| dog bone Outside | 15, named / 0 | 26, none named / 0 | 0 / 0 |\n\nThe tried level blend of #3934 gave 35 lifts on the disc and 24 crossing feeds on the dog bone. The kernel gives 0 crossing feeds. The first head of this PR read 0 lifts on Outside too, but only because the edge strip counted as open ground, which is not proved. Outside starts at the stock edge. The link from one piece there to the next runs over the strip that the next piece cuts, and the kernel cannot leave the stock into the air (its air starts one tool radius outside the stock). Follow-up: #4241.\n\nLaw suite: 0 lifts on the disc pocket (Auto, Inside, Outside) and on the two bands Inside. The disc band lifts 13 times on Auto and Outside (5 `CROSSES_CUT`, 4 `UNCUT_STOCK`, 4 `CUTS_PART`). The dog-bone band lifts 15 times on Auto and Outside (13 `CROSSES_CUT`, 2 `UNCUT_STOCK`). The pocket with an island has 7 lifts (Inside and Auto) and 5 lifts (Outside), each with a named reason:\n- Inside: the four corners are four separate deepest areas. The link between two corners runs over a strip that is not cut yet, or across a ring that is still planned.\n- Outside: the walk must go from the wall rings to the island rings, across the rings that are still planned between them.\n\nThe engagement readings are higher than the old ones (for example `over 3504` on the disc Inside: the rings run outward from the part wall, and each move of the dense rings counts). This step does not change the load. Load control is K3.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/pathkernel/tests/laws/order_link.rs`:\n  - `k4_order_obeys_l3_with_the_ring_planner`\n  - `k4_link_rule_holds_and_each_lift_is_named` (pins the lift counts)\n  - `a_link_across_the_island_is_refused_with_the_part_reason`\n  - `a_link_round_the_island_stays_on_cut_ground_only`\n  - `a_lift_with_no_reason_is_refused_and_a_retract_is_named`\n  - `an_order_that_moves_a_curve_is_refused`\n  - `the_side_orders_the_rings_and_climb_keeps_the_material_on_the_right`\n  - `the_marks_go_with_their_curves_and_a_full_width_stretch_is_cut_last`\n  - `a_link_along_the_stock_edge_over_uncut_stock_is_refused` (review fix)\n  - `a_whole_full_width_curve_is_cut_after_the_other_ready_curves` (review fix)\n  - `a_row_on_the_first_step_keeps_its_direction_and_the_next_rows_zigzag` (review fix)\n- `crates/motion/tests/kernel_laws/k4_order_link.rs`: `kernel_order_and_link_round_the_disc_and_the_dog_bone` (0 crossings, named lifts equal to the lifts, tally equal to the lifts, the lift counts).\n- `crates/geometry/src/geo2d/segments.rs` unit tests, and `link::route` unit tests.\n\n## Gates (final head d50f14a54)\n\n- Quick gate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/side/path-kernel` (25f3838db). The geometry change reaches every crate, so the plan is the full batch. Result: 1223 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, wall 73.9 min. It includes clippy `-D warnings`, `pathkernel suites: laws`, `motion suites: kernel_laws` and `app suites: example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive` and `example_catalog_edge_work`, all ok.\n- Separately on the same tree: `cargo check --tests` for `camcraft-pathkernel` and `camcraft-motion`; `laws` 125 passed; pathkernel lib 5 passed; `kernel_laws` 29 passed; clippy `-D warnings` on pathkernel and motion, clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light` ran on the first head (7 steps, 0 failed). The review fix changes only the kernel, which no planner calls yet, so the light twins do not reach it. Not run again.\n\n## Decisions\n\n`docs/decisions/4177-kernel-order-link.md` has the decisions in full. In short:\n- A full-width stretch is cut last: last of the ready curves, and a closed curve starts where its longest full-width stretch ends.\n- The sense of the walk comes from the region.\n- Climb keeps the uncut material on the right.\n- The edge strip of the stock is stock: open only where the swath of a made cut covers it (the `AIR` margin is removed).\n- A curve that is full-width as a whole comes after the other ready curves and starts as a plain curve. A row on the first step is never reversed.\n- These were not ported: the lifted joins of `air_links`, and the stay-down length limit.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Rows (Zigzag): one order pin (first row and zigzag) on hand-made rows, none with the row planner. The Fallback note for a start side on Zigzag is not added.\n- Exact circle rings and `RingRef::Band`: both are still refused by K2.\n- Keep-out areas (`HITS_FIXTURE`): no fixture pin.\n- The order stage runs the link proof on each step. Its cost on large parts is not measured.\n- No app or UI path calls the kernel yet.\n\nNew top-level test files: none. The pins join the `laws` suite and the `kernel_laws` suite.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nEffort: max\n\nRefs #4177\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
